<section class="hero capability-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Capabilities</p>
  <h1>Native tracked changes for agent-driven Word workflows.</h1>
  <p>
    Read, edit, compare, comment on, and review existing document files with explicit
    boundaries around what Safe DOCX edits, redlines, or only preserves.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="cta" href="#capability-matrix">Explore capabilities</a>
    <a class="cta cta-ghost" href="../index.html#install">Install Safe DOCX</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="capability-principle reveal" aria-labelledby="claim-model-heading">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">How to read this page</p>
    <h2 id="claim-model-heading">Preserved does not automatically mean compared.</h2>
  </div>
  <p>
    Word documents contain independent stories and package parts. Safe DOCX may preserve a
    header, field, or endnote safely without yet turning changes inside it into tracked
    revisions. This page names those boundaries instead of collapsing them into one
    “supported” claim.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="capability-legend reveal" aria-label="Capability status legend">
